  "intro": {
    "cards": [
      {
        "title": "What it is",
        "body": "Present simple is for **habits**, **routines**, and **facts** — not only “right now”.",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Use",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "habit / routine",
              "I **work** every day."
            ],
            [
              "fact",
              "Water **boils** at 100°C."
            ],
            [
              "with time words",
              "She **goes** on Mondays."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Form",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Subject",
            "positive",
            "negative"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "I / you / we / they",
              "work",
              "don't work"
            ],
            [
              "he / she / it",
              "works",
              "doesn't work"
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "he/she/it → **-s** in the positive: works · likes · goes · has",
          "Negatives: see next card"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Negatives",
        "body": "Use **do / does** + **not** + base verb. Short forms are common in speech.",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Subject",
            "negative",
            "short"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "I / you / we / they",
              "do not work",
              "don't work"
            ],
            [
              "he / she / it",
              "does not work",
              "doesn't work"
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "After *don't / doesn't*, the main verb has **no -s**: She doesn't **work** (not *works*)",
          "he/she/it → **doesn't** · I/you/we/they → **don't**",
          "Not: *She not work* · *He don't like*"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "When",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Signal",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "every day / week",
              "I study every evening."
            ],
            [
              "usually / often / always",
              "He usually walks."
            ],
            [
              "on Mondays · at weekends",
              "We play on Sunday."
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "Not the main form for “happening now” (that is often present continuous later)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Common mistakes",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Avoid",
            "Say"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "He **work** here.",
              "He **works** here."
            ],
            [
              "She **don't** like tea.",
              "She **doesn't** like tea."
            ],
            [
              "I **am work** every day.",
              "I **work** every day."
            ],
            [
              "They **works** in Brno.",
              "They **work** in Brno."
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "Missing **-s** after he/she/it",
          "don't vs **doesn't**"
        ]
      },
